  "raw": {
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=2911": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry Job Department/School Chemistry FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Chemistry College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The Chemistry department at Adelphi University invites applications for adjunct faculty (part-time) positions. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,866 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . RESPONSIBILITIES: The successful candidate will be expected to teach general chemistry laboratory, or organic chemistry laboratory. QUALIFICATIONS: An advanced degree in any area of chemistry or a closely-related, chemistry-intensive field is required. A Ph.D. in any area of chemistry or a closely-related, chemistry-intensive field is preferred. APPLICATION: Applications must include a cover letter, a teaching philosophy, CV and transcript. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . For more information about the ACS-approved chemistry department, go to: http://chemistry.adelphi.edu . ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving almost 8,000 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers more than 60 undergraduate programs, more than 65 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and more than 35 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 116,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 64 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. College of Arts and Sciences: The College of Arts and Sciences at Adelphi University is a community of educators, learners, and citizens firmly committed to the principles of diversity, equity, and inclusion. We believe that these principles enrich our entire community, foster healthy discussions, improve decision-making, and enhance the educational environment and outcomes of our students. We support initiatives, activities, discussions, and practices that uphold the equitable treatment of all members of our community and strengthen their sense of belonging at Adelphi. We relentlessly strive to become a model for a socially just and inclusive institution. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3413": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Cultural Anthropology and Political Economy",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Cultural Anthropology and Political Economy Job Department/School College of Arts and Sciences FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Levermore Global Scholars Program Anthropology Department College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The Levermore Global Scholars Program and the department of Anthropology, Adelphi University, New York, invite applications for a part-time faculty position beginning in January 2027. While the geographic and research areas are open, the department seeks a candidate with experience teaching introductory Cultural Anthropology, Political Economy, and/or First Year and Senior Year college seminars from a global perspective. The candidate should be prepared to teach two sections a semester. QUALIFICATIONS: A master's degree in Anthropology is required. Applicants actively pursing a Ph.D are preferred. APPLICATION: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, current CV, and the name and contact information for two references. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . Applications will be considered until the position is filled. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,937 per credit. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi is one of just four companies and the only university on Long Island to be named among America’s Best Employers by State for 2023 by Forbes. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,400 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Brooklyn, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 70 undergraduate programs, 93 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 64 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 44 states and 76 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3327": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing and Public Heallth",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Nursing and Public Heallth Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: The College of Nursing and Public Health at Adelphi University is seeking adjunct professors for the fall 2026 and spring 2027 semesters (at both our Garden City, NY and Manhattan extension center locations). At the Adelphi University College of Nursing and Public Health, we educate the next generation of healthcare professionals to be committed to excellence as leaders in their disciplines. Our innovative evidence-based teaching and learning environments, combined with our collaborative healthcare and community partnerships, prepare students at all levels. Students will attain the necessary knowledge and interdisciplinary skills to excel as caring practitioners, health informaticists, scientists and scholars. RESPONSIBILITIES: Adjunct faculty will provide part-time instruction to students, hired on a per-course/per-semester basis and will adhere to all Adelphi Faculty policies and procedures, as defined in the Faculty Handbook. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Current Registered Nurse licensed in the State of New York is required. Master’s degree in Nursing is required. Minimum of five years of practice experience in specialty area (e.g. Adult Health, Pediatrics, OB etc.). Current BLS certification if teaching clinical. Current teaching experience; ability to teach across undergraduate and/or graduate curricula. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Strong interpersonal skills and ability to relate to students. Effective time management skills. Effective written communication skills. Project a professional and appropriate demeanor when interacting with colleagues and students. Provide useful feedback to students regarding their coursework and performance. APPLICATION: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter and a current CV with references directly on the Adelphi site to be considered. Direct any inquiries to Lena Garafalo (CNPH Adjunct Faculty Coordinator, lgarafalo@adelphi.edu ) and Sheryl Rosenberg ( smrosenberg@adelphi.edu ). SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,937 per credit. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi is one of just four companies and the only university on Long Island to be named among America’s Best Employers by State for 2023 by Forbes. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,400 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Brooklyn, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 70 undergraduate programs, 93 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 64 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 44 states and 76 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE COLLEGE OF NURSING AND PUBLIC HEALTH: At the Adelphi University College of Nursing and Public Health, we educate the next generation of healthcare professionals to be committed to excellence as leaders in their disciplines. Our innovative evidence-based teaching and learning environments, combined with our collaborative healthcare and community partnerships, prepare students at all levels. Students will attain the necessary knowledge and interdisciplinary skills to excel as caring practitioners, health informaticists, scientists and scholars. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3085": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psych Mental Health NP Program",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Psych Mental Health NP Program Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Psych Mental Health NP Program College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: As an adjunct faculty member in Adelphi University's esteemed PMHNP Masters of Science program, you will empower students to unlock their fullest potential. Join us on this rewarding path. The Adelphi PMHNP program is acclaimed for its commitment to rigor while supporting student success. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching specialty didactic and clinical courses. Assessing clinical competencies and theoretical knowledge while supporting comprehensive learning. Provide mentorship to the next generation of PMHNPs. REQUIREMENTS: Earned PMHNP master's degree or a post-graduate certificate. ANCC board certification as a PMHNP. A current, unrestricted NYS PMHNP license. Two or more years’ experience treating patients as a PMHNP. A background in education, whether through formal teaching roles or as a preceptor is preferred, but not required. Earned DNP, PhD, or other terminal degree is preferred, but not required. APPLICATION: Interested applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter outlining qualifications and teaching experience. A Curriculum Vitae (CV) detailing relevant academic and professional experience. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,866 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
