    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3401": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and MSW Program Director",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and MSW Program Director Job Department/School Social Work FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and MSW Program Director School of Social Work JOB SUMMARY: The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs provides oversight and leadership for the MSW and BSW programs in academic standards, explicit and implicit curriculum design and implementation, faculty development, academic affairs, and student achievement. This oversight extends to all program options (OMSW, Garden City, Poughkeepsie, Middletown, Hauppauge and NYC). The ADAA supervises the director of the BSW programs, the coordinator of the OMSW program, and the directors of Practicum Education and Student Affairs. The ADAA works in concert with the Center coordinators in the planning of center activities and focus areas. The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs consults with faculty around course assignments, hires and evaluates adjunct faculty, oversees and approves course schedules, and assigns faculty to courses within MSW program. The ADAA will explore areas for SSW growth and development, including flexible learning options, develop collaborations with state and community agencies, and identify and pursue federal training grants. This role also includes being the director of the MSW Program. While there is a strong relationship of the responsibilities of the MSW Program Director and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs specific responsibilities of the MSW Program Director position entail operationalizing key accreditation standards related to the MSW program’s curriculum processes and objectives, addressing student retention, academic progress, and degree completion. The MSW program director plans orientations for adjunct faculty, plans course scheduling, and monitors the implementation of the curriculum. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $140,000 - $170,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . REPORTS TO: Dean of the School of Social Work RESPONSIBILITIES & DUTIES: Ensures quality and integrity of the MSW, OMSW and BSW programs across all program locations: Provide leadership and supervision to the Director of Practicum Education, Director of Student Affairs, Coordinator of the OMSW Program, and Director of the BSW Program. Oversees the revision and updating of the BSW and MSW Student Handbook and Practicum Education Handbook to assure clear articulation of academic policies and educational processes, and consistency across school and university publications; Provide direction and leadership of academic administrators and administrative support staff responding to requests for exception to academic policies, preparing and tracking academic petitions for leaves of absence, withdrawals, late drops, etc. for BSW and MSW program; Provide oversight of assessment of students on leaves of absence to determine suitability for the return to the program; Work with Director of Practicum Education to address challenges in students’ progress toward foundation and advanced level competence; Facilitate communication and problem resolution in addressing academic-related concerns identified by students and/or their professors; Respond to student grievances in accordance with established school and university policies. Design, implement and maintain systems and procedures for working with students at academic risk: Oversee implementation of academic standards including development of academic probation contracts; Direct academic affairs administrators and administrative support staff in tracking and notification of students with low GPAs, students on probation or at-risk within the MSW program; Oversee processes around allegations of plagiarism and other forms of academic dishonesty and interpret policy and procedures, collect and file forms and evidence of plagiarism, refer egregious or repeat offenders to the Academic Standards Committee, consistent with School and University policies; Provide leadership to faculty, academic advisors, and the practicum education department around policies and procedures in the School of Social Work related to academic standards within the BSW and MSW programs; Develop and implement protocols to identify academically at-risk students to promote positive student outcomes. Curriculum design and implementation for the MSW program at all locations: Provide leadership in the delivery of a coherent and integrated explicit and implicit curriculum for class and practicum education; Consult with Curriculum Committee on curriculum implementation, curriculum renewal, and adjunct faculty development; Plan course offerings for all program sites within established time frames and in accordance with policy and procedures provided by the Office of the Provost and University Registrar; Consult with faculty around course assignments and assign faculty to classes, collaborating with Center Coordinators and other stakeholders as necessary; Provide guidance to the Chair of the Curriculum Committee to ensure that all curricula effectively operationalize the core competencies at the foundation and advanced levels and that all course syllabi are up to date and comport with established school, university, and accreditation standards; Provide leadership around licensing preparation and outcomes associated with the implicit and explicit curriculum and work with faculty to integrate licensing preparation within the curriculum. Student Advisement and Registration: Direct the academic affairs administrative team to prepare and disseminate program and advisement materials to support academic advisement processes that are responsive to the differential needs of the School’s diverse student body; Direct academic affairs administrators, center coordinators, and practicum education administrators to implement advisement and registration procedures; Liaison with University offices to assure integrity of registration processes and implementation of student academic affairs policies and processes; Direct academic affairs administrators and administrative support staff to ensure compliance with academic clearance processes for graduation from the MSW program. Student Affairs: Provide supervision and oversight to the Director of Student Affairs and Director of Practicum Education to promote the development of student activities and student engagement that is responsive to the differential needs of the School’s diverse student body at all program locations; Supervise and collaborate with administration and faculty to promote opportunities for student participation in formulating and modifying policies affecting academic and student affairs. Coordinate academic supports through external (University) resources for BSW and MSW students (e.g., Student Access, Counseling Services, writing and statistic tutors, career services). Committee Membership: Member of Dean’s Administrators’ Team Member of SSW Curriculum Committee (ex-officio) Member (ex-officio) of the Self-Study/Accreditation Committee related to implementation of the CSWE  Educational Policy and Accreditation Standards (EPAS) Member of the Practicum Education Committee Member (ex-officio) of the Assessment Committee Perform other duties as assigned. REQUIREMENTS: (Knowledge, Skills and Abilities) Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience in public speaking. Strong identification with the purposes and values of the social work profession and a demonstrated commitment to social justice. Experience in social work education, including demonstrated leadership skills through committee work and other activities. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively with a diverse student body, faculty, administration, and staff. Ability to manage time in a fast-paced office environment, and to work on multiple projects simultaneously. Comprehensive knowledge of graduate social work education, current and emerging trends in social curriculum and social work practice. Strong management and organizational skills. Commitment to competence in using administrative and instructional technology. EDUCATIONAL/EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS: M.S.W. and doctorate in social work or an allied field is required. Minimum of 10 years post-master’s practice, teaching, and administrative experience is required. POSITION(S) SUPERVISED: Director of Student Affairs. Director of Practicum Education. Director of the BSW Program. Coordinator of the OMSW Program. Hourly Clerical Staff as assigned. HOW TO APPLY: To be considered, candidates must apply on the Adelphi website: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . When applying please upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae. Letter of application (letter should include 1) academic leadership experience, 2) familiarity with master's and baccalaureate social work curriculum and accreditation standards, and 3) experience developing state and community collaborations). Names and contact information of three (3) references. (No actual letters. References will not be contacted without prior permission of the candidate). Three (3) representative publications. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3436": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Art Education",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Art Education Job Department/School College of Arts and Sciences FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Art and Art History College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The Department of Art and Art History at Adelphi University invites applications for a new tenure-track position in Art Education, starting Fall 2026. Applicants should have a terminal degree in art education or a related field, such as a PhD or EdD in Art Education. The position will be at the rank of Assistant Professor. This Assistant Professor of Art Education role involves teaching undergraduate art education courses, mentoring students, supervising student teachers, and developing curriculum. It also includes engaging in research, creative activities, and service to the department, institution, and the art education community. The position works closely with the Art and Art History program, especially the Studio Art BFA program and its faculty. Key duties include curriculum design, promoting student success in diverse classrooms, maintaining scholarly or creative work, participating in faculty governance, and collaborating on interdisciplinary projects. RESPONSIBILITIES: Administrative tasks may include overseeing undergraduate programs in Art Education, participating in New York State Board of Education program reviews, interacting with schools, communities, and constituencies, and developing collaborative programs within the studio art department. Candidates may also take on placement coordinator duties. Candidates are expected to maintain professional scholarly or creative output, represent the department in local, regional, and national forums, and contribute service to the department, institution, and community. Experience working with diverse populations is valued, particularly supporting students through coursework differentiation and accommodations, sharing successful teaching strategies, and fostering a caring, productive classroom environment. Core Responsibilities: Teaching and Curriculum: Deliver undergraduate and graduate courses, including methods and licensure classes. Student Mentorship & Supervision: Advise and mentor students, supervise student teaching and practical experiences, and support student career development. Curriculum Development: Create new curricula and improve existing ones. Research & Creative Activity: Participate in research, creative production, and scholarly efforts that advance the field of art education. QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates should hold a terminal degree in art education or a related discipline, such as an MFA, PhD or EdD. The ideal candidate will be prepared to teach art education seminars and core courses in the undergraduate program (including licensure courses), develop and refine curricula, supervise thesis projects and fieldwork, and advise students pursuing careers in art education and related fields. Applicants should have at least five years of teaching experience in K-12 education, along with three years of teaching at the academic level . APPLICATION: Candidates must submit the following materials: A cover letter explaining your interest in and qualifications for the position (2-3 pages). A current curriculum vitae. A teaching statement (1-2 pages). Two examples of course syllabi. An artist’s statement (1-2 pages). A PDF portfolio showcasing recent professional studio art practice or examples of creative research. Teaching evaluations and/or observations. Three references (NOTE: letters or phone calls of references will be requested later, and referees will need to submit them within three weeks). To be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website only: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . This appointment is subject to final approval by the Adelphi University Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $77,000 - $82,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3437": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Clinical Psychology Job Department/School Derner School of Psychology FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Clinical Psychology Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology JOB SUMMARY: The Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology at Adelphi University seeks to enhance its roster of distinguished faculty through the addition of a colleague with a strong background in clinical psychology. We are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to teaching undergraduate and graduate students from diverse cultural backgrounds. RESPONSIBILITIES: Candidates will be expected to contribute to our APA accredited Ph.D. program in clinical psychology in terms of teaching, scholarship, research and service, equally. In addition to teaching courses in clinical psychology, broadly defined, applicants will mentor and advise Ph.D. and M.A. students. Teaching and advising across programs in the Derner School of Psychology. QUALIFICATIONS: Applicants for this tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor must have a Ph.D. or Psy.D. and will begin teaching no later than the Fall 2027 semester. Applicants with a strong publication record would be preferred. Research and scholarship involving psychopathology and/or psychotherapy is required (open to candidates of any theoretical orientation). Applicants must be licensed as a Psychologist or eligible for licensure in NY State. APPLICATION: Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research interests, selected reprints/preprints (a maximum of 3), evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available), and three letters of recommendations. Please submit application materials by January 2 nd . Review of applications will be conducted on an ongoing basis until the position is filled. Questions should be forwarded to Associate Professor Michael Moore, Chair of the Search Committee, at mmoore@adelphi.edu. To be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/open-positions/ . This appointment is subject to final approval by the Adelphi University Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE GORDON F. DERNER SCHOOL OF PSYCHOLOGY: The Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology is committed to having a diverse and inclusive faculty and thus especially invites applications from historically disadvantaged groups.  We are committed to achieving excellence through cultural diversity.  For further information about the Derner School of Psychology which includes an APA approved Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology, a School Psychology Psy.D., and M.A. programs in General Psychology, School Psychology, and Mental Health Counseling, and post-graduate programs as well as one of the largest undergraduate majors at Adelphi, please click here for more information: https://derner.adelphi.edu . The Clinical Psychology Ph.D. Program is an integrative, empirically-informed program with a long psychoanalytic tradition and commitment to social justice. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $85,000 - $95,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3432": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Physical Chemistry or Biochemistry",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Physical Chemistry or Biochemistry Job Department/School College of Arts and Sciences FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Chemistry College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: Adelphi University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in chemistry that begins August 2027.  A Ph.D. in chemistry or a related field is required; additional post-doctoral or industrial experience is desired. Preference will be given to applicants that are biochemists or physical chemists.  The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in general chemistry, physical chemistry or biochemistry, and on occasion advanced courses related to one’s field.  Our new colleague will join an ACS-approved program where undergraduate research is embedded into our culture. The successful candidate must therefore also be committed to establishing a high-quality research program with undergraduate researchers and be committed to becoming an outstanding teacher. We are especially interested in candidates from historically underrepresented communities and candidates who can help the department make the educational experience more inclusive for our diverse student populations . RESPONSIBILITIES: The teaching load is 18 credits with opportunities for research release.  Our new colleague will teach undergraduate courses including lectures and laboratories. The primary teaching assignment will be general chemistry, and biochemistry or physical chemistry.  Other teaching responsibilities will include special topics courses related to their field. The successful candidate will be expected to build and sustain an ongoing record of research with undergraduate students from diverse cultural backgrounds that will result in peer-reviewed publications and presentations by students at national meetings. The successful candidate will contribute to service duties within the department, college, university, and at professional levels; engage in the mentoring and advising of chemistry and biochemistry majors; attend our weekly chemistry seminar along with the rest of our faculty members and majors; and collaborate with other faculty across the STEM disciplines. QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates should have earned a Ph.D. in chemistry or a or a closely related, chemistry-intensive field.  Additional post-doctoral or industrial experience is preferred. Applicants must demonstrate a commitment to the University’s goal of improving higher education for diverse and underrepresented students. We have a strong interest in ensuring that all candidates hired for faculty appointments share our commitment to educational access, equity, excellence, and diversity. APPLICATION: Interested candidates must submit the following materials online at https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ to be considered. Cover letter (maximum two-pages double-spaced) that explains why you are an excellent candidate for the job, why specifically you want to work at Adelphi, and anything other relevant information. Any candidate that is a tenure-track or tenured professor at another institution must explain why they desire to move to Adelphi. Curriculum vitae. On the last page, please provide the names and email addresses of three academic references willing to write you a letter of recommendation. We will handle requesting the letters. Statement of teaching philosophy-maximum two-pages double-spaced. Research proposal appropriate for involving undergraduate students that is 3-7 pages double-spaced.  References do not count towards the page limit. You must include a section titled “ Research with Undergraduates” where you discuss how undergraduates can be involved in your research and that you understand that there are not graduate students in the chemistry department of Adelphi University. We do not require transcripts in the application, but you will be expected to provide an official graduate transcript if you are invited for an in-person interview. For questions, inquiries may be directed to Professor Dan Silverio, Associate Professor, Chair, Search Committee, at dsilverio@adelphi.edu. Review of applications will begin Nov 9, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. If the position is still posted on the Adelphi site, the position has not been filled. This appointment is subject to final approval by the Adelphi University Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. For further information about the department of chemistry , please visit our website: http://chemistry.adelphi.edu . For chemistry instrumentation, see https://www.adelphi.edu/arts-sciences/stem/chemistry/labs/ . SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $77,000 - $82,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3441": {
      "title": "Director of Derner Professional Programs - NYC",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Director of Derner Professional Programs - NYC Job Department/School Derner School of Psychology FT/PT/Temp Full time Location New York City Apply Now Director of Derner Professional Programs in NYC Clinical Faculty, Open Rank Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology JOB SUMMARY: The Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology at Adelphi University invites applications for a full-time clinical faculty position, at open rank, to serve as Director of Derner Professional Programs in NYC. The position will be based primarily at Adelphi’s Manhattan Center and will combine teaching and clinical expertise with administrative leadership for Derner’s professional programs and clinical activities in New York City. We seek an accomplished clinician-educator with disciplinary expertise relevant to Derner’s professional training programs and demonstrated potential for academic and administrative leadership and innovation. The successful candidate will contribute to Derner’s mission to integrate clinical and theoretical work through teaching, coordination, supervision, and development of professional training initiatives at the Manhattan Center. RESPONSIBILITIES: The Director will provide academic and administrative leadership for Derner’s professional programs and clinical training activities in New York City. Initial responsibilities will include: Providing leadership and oversight for clinical activities at the Manhattan Center, including supervision and coordination of clinical training involving students in Derner’s PhD Program in Clinical Psychology. Working closely with doctoral program leadership, faculty, and administrative staff to ensure the quality, coordination, and appropriate oversight of clinical services and training. Leading the development and implementation of programming for Derner’s Master’s Program in Mental Health Counseling (MHC) at the Manhattan Center. Developing relationships with clinical, educational, and community partners throughout New York City to expand our clinic through assessment, therapy and research integration. Collaborating with the Deans, program directors, faculty, and University leadership in strategic planning for the growth and visibility of Derner’s NYC presence. Contributing to the longer-term development of additional professional, clinical, and continuing-education initiatives in New York City. Teaching courses consistent with the candidate’s area of disciplinary and clinical expertise. Recruiting, coordinating, and supporting faculty and supervisors associated with Manhattan-based programming, as appropriate. Participating in School and University service consistent with a clinical faculty appointment. QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must possess a doctoral degree in clinical or counseling psychology. New York State licensure as a psychologist is required. Three to five years of experience post-licensure is required. Prior experience directing or administering a clinical service, training program, academic program, or comparable professional initiative is desirable. Rank will be determined based on the successful candidate’s qualifications and professional accomplishments. Candidates should demonstrate: Strong disciplinary and clinical expertise relevant to graduate professional education; A record of excellence in clinical teaching, supervision of multidisciplinary teams, and/or professional training; Experience with, or clear capacity for, academic or clinical administration; The organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills necessary to coordinate faculty, students, clinical activities, and program development; Commitment to high-quality professional education and clinical training; Ability to work collaboratively across programs and with internal and external partners; Interest in developing innovative professional and academic programming responsive to the opportunities afforded by a New York City location. APPLICATION: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, and a list of three professional references. To be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/open-positions/ . This appointment is subject to final approval by the Adelphi University Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE GORDON F. DERNER SCHOOL OF PSYCHOLOGY: The Gordon F. Derner School of Psychology has a distinguished history in psychological science, clinical training, and professional education. Its programs span undergraduate through postdoctoral education and reflect longstanding strengths in clinical psychology, psychotherapy, psychological assessment, mental health counseling, and related areas of psychological science and practice. The Director of Derner Professional Programs in NYC will play an important role in advancing the school’s professional training mission and building a distinctive Derner presence at Adelphi University’s Manhattan Center. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $105,000 - $135,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3440": {
      "title": "Director of the Occupational Therapy Program",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Director of the Occupational Therapy Program Job Department/School College of Education and Health Sciences FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Director of the Occupational Therapy Program Ruth S. Ammon College of Education and Health Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The Ruth S. Ammon College of Education and Health Sciences at Adelphi University is pleased to invite applications for the position of Inaugural Director for the Occupational Therapy Program to be based in Adelphi’s new Manhattan Center. This position is at the Associate or Full Professor level. The Director of Occupational Therapy (OT) provides overall leadership and administrative oversight for the OT program, ensuring the program meets and exceeds the standards set by the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE). This role involves leading the development, implementation, and management of the program's curriculum and operations, fostering a positive learning environment, and ensuring the success of students. The successful candidate will be based at the new Manhattan Center. RESPONSIBILITIES: Be responsible for creation, development, accreditation, operationalization, and management of a new OT program at Adelphi University and envision what distinguishes the program in the NYC market. Lead and be responsible for development of all ACOTE-required accreditation candidacy documents, and oversight of all ongoing accreditation assessment and compliance. Oversee the design, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of the curriculum. Have a background in clinical practice, as well as deep experience in teaching and academic administration Assist with hiring, orientation, and supervision of faculty and staff involved with the program, demonstrating responsiveness to issues related to personnel, leadership, program development, accreditation, and program assessment. Participate in evaluation of student performance and academic counseling of students. Demonstrate evidence of teaching and curriculum expertise, faculty development and mentorship competencies, as well as enthusiasm for inter-professional collaboration. Manage the program's budget and ensure appropriate resources are available to support its operations. Develop, expand, and maintain affiliations with clinical sites to provide high-quality clinical experiences for students. QUALIFICATIONS: Licensure as an Occupational Therapist in NY State with a minimum of five years of recent clinical experience practicing as an OT. Relevant doctoral degree is preferred. Experience in academic administration, health professions teaching, and faculty development, minimum of three years. Knowledge of and experience with healthcare regulations, standards, and the accreditation process for OT programs. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. APPLICATION: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, with a list of three professional references, and a Teaching Statement. To be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website ( https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/open-positions/ ). This appointment is subject to final approval by the Adelphi University Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for the Associate Professor level is $100,000 - $125,000 and the annual base salary range for the Full Professor level is $120,000 - $155,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    }
  },
